computations:
Who an order waits on, from x = J.stepOf(j):
• held or struck by a team member → that person;
• held by ‘The client’ → j.client;
• rest → a timed wait of x.who;
• run → running by itself.
At 09:41:
• 6 with the team: Nakhla, Board breakfast and Graduation dinner (Reem); Wedding lunch (Hala); Family dinner (Salma); Meetup coffee break (Yusuf).
• 1 with a client: Charity dinner (Rania).
• 3 by themselves: Engagement lunch (the receipt), Office lunch (the two-day wait), Book launch reception (the invoice).

Reminder text: V.fill(step.msg, j) replaces:
• {client.name} with j.client;
• {order.title} with j.title;
• {quote.link} with 'sufra.iqaa.app/q/' + j.code.slice(-4).
It is shown exactly as it would go out.

Durations in words, V.span(ms):
• from 1 day: ‘N days and M hours’ (M left out when 0) below 7 days; ‘N days’ from 7;
• ‘N hours’ (floored) from 2 hours;
• ‘an hour and M minutes’;
• ‘M minutes’.
Examples: 20 h 22 min → ‘20 hours’; 1 h 11 min → ‘an hour and 11 minutes’; 4 d 3 h → ‘4 days and 3 hours’.
Data cells use ‘7 d 23 h’ in mono.

accessibility:
Focus:
• stays in the composer after asking;
• Approve moves it to the draft’s new status line (tabindex -1) and announces ‘Approved: remind Omar now’;
• Discard moves it to Undo;
• rail rows and the strip’s Show move it to the draft’s h3.

Contrast, measured on white:
• ink 17.45:1;
• n700 8.16:1 for secondary text;
• n600 5.65:1, the faintest text;
• violet text only on white or n50 (4.94 / 4.51:1), never on n100 (4.12:1);
• dashed rails and pens in n500, 3.95:1 on white and 3.62:1 on n50 (the non-text minimum is 3:1);
• white on violet 4.94:1 for Approve.

