CREATE assets/js/watar.js (about 650 lines):
• setup (viewer from ?as=, demo clock, storage);
• the lexicon built from S;
• ask(text, ctx), pure;
• part renderers (rows, time strip, one order, mini rows, stations, station, done, lead time);
• drafts (approve, discard, take back, replace, change the time, line handoff);
• the composer;
• the rail and the narrow strip (IntersectionObserver);
• ?q= handling;
• the live region;
• updates to data-n-watar and the phone dot;
• sets [data-me-*] for ?as= before app.js runs, as today.js does.

CREATE assets/css/watar.css:
• .aw- rules only: head, body grid and container queries, turns, figure, time strip, mini rows (copied from today.css’s .mn, because loading today.css would clash on .dn and .dn-t), drafts with the dashed rail, choices, composer band and field, rail, strip, disclosure;
• .aw .g.running svg { animation: tick var(--m-beat) step-end infinite } plus its reduced-motion off (the keyframes are in auth.css).

CREATE research/qa-watar.html — the qa-today.html pattern:
• an iframe at w × h loading watar.html?q=&as=;
• do= approve, discard, line (clicks ‘Draft it on the Line screen’, so the capture shows line.html with the draft), new, scroll (y);
• the same transition-off style, the late resize event and the blur.

CHANGE assets/js/jobs.js — inside views(J, S) add:
• T, fmt, hm and dayName (UTC wall clock);
• delivered and late (from overview.js);
• restHours and REST (line.js’s five lengths);
• clock(j) (order.js’s spread, plus pins, open arch and UTC);
• journey(j, c) (moved from order.js unchanged, states from c);
• dueRow(j) (overview.js’s att() moved unchanged);
• risk(j, now), fill(msg, j) and span(ms).
Return them all.

